    <row>
        <cell>Archie is learning to scuba dive.  The equation <m>D(L)</m> represents the depth, <m>D</m> he can dive, in feet, based on the number of lessons, <m>L</m> he has taken.  How deep can Archie dive after he has taken 13 lessons?</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
        <cell>Stormy joins a gym.  She pays $15 for the membership and $6 for each session she does at the gym.  Write and equation that models the relationship between the cost <m>C</m> that STormy pays, and the number of sessions <m>n</m> that she does at the gym.  Write the equation in function notation,</cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
    <row>
        <cell>Michael is draining his pool for the winter,  There are 3200 gallons of water in the pool and it is decreasing at a rate of 200 gallons per hour.  Write an equation to represent the relationship between the amount of water <m>A</m> in the pool, and the number of hours <m>h</m> the poos has been draining.  Write the equation in function notation.</cell>
        <cell>---</cell>
        <cell> </cell>
    </row>
    <row>
        <cell>Mama B is planning Thanksgiving dinner.  The number of pounds of turkey she will buy depends on the number of people she invites to dinner.  If she invites 9 people, she needs to buy a 15 pound turkey.  If she invites 12 people, she needs to buy a 20 pound turkey.  WRite an equation to represent the relationshp between the number of people <m>p</m> and the pounds <m>P</m> of turkey needed.  Write the equation in function notation.</cell>
